# PlatformIO
.pio/

# Editor settings
.vscode/
.claude/

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local notes
031226.txt
CLAUDE.md
tasks/lessons.md
tasks/todo.md
# Session working notes are local by design. They accumulate the machine
# names, serial ports, device addresses and bench forensics of whoever ran
# the session, none of which belongs in a public repository. Durable
# lessons get lifted into docs/ instead; see docs/build-and-bench-notes.md.
tasks/*.md
/HANDOFF-*.md

# Local vendor/reference clones
.vendor/

# Release/build artifacts
#
# Anchored, per the /content/ note at the bottom of this file: a bare
# "firmware/" matches a directory of that name at ANY depth. Today the only
# other match is web/firmware/, which is ignored deliberately a few lines down,
# so the bare form happened to be harmless - but it is the same trap that
# swallowed src/content/, waiting for anyone who adds a src/firmware/.
#
# Note the asymmetry with keys/ below: build-output patterns are anchored so
# they cannot reach into source, while a SECRETS pattern is deliberately left
# unanchored so it matches at every depth. For ignores, being too narrow leaks;
# for build output, being too broad hides source.
/firmware/
HexHound-Firmware-*.zip
sim-build.log
serial_test_build.log
*build_flags.txt
__pycache__/

# Web flasher build output (staged by scripts/stage_web_flasher.py)
web/firmware/
web/manifests/
web/boards.json

# Content-pack signing keys. The PRIVATE half of a content signing key must
# never be committed: anyone holding it can mint content that every device
# carrying the matching public key accepts. Only the PUBLIC half belongs in
# the tree, and it lives in src/content/content_pubkey.h as source.
keys/
*.key
!*.pub.key

# Signed content packs are build output of scripts/sign_content_pack.py, not
# source. The authored JSON under content-src/ is the source.
data/content/*.hcp

# Local agent/tool scratch
.codex/
.playwright-mcp/

# Backups left behind by the framework patch scripts
*.orig

# Signed content packs are build output: authored source lives in content-src/
# and the signed .hcp files are produced by scripts/sign_content_pack.py.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Without it this pattern matches a directory
# named "content" at ANY depth, which silently swallowed the whole of
# src/content/: content_crypto, content_cbor, content_pack and content_pubkey
# were on disk and building locally while being invisible to git. The P3-W1
# commit therefore pushed a main that no fresh clone could compile, and the
# "green suites" that vouched for it were green only on the one machine that
# still had the untracked files. Anchor build-output patterns to the repo root.
/content/

# Contact sheet from `gen_wear_anchors.py --preview`. A verification artifact,
# regenerated on demand from the art and the table, so it is not history.
/wear_anchors_preview.png

# Demo recordings from `scripts/make_demo_video.py`. Regenerated on demand from
# the simulator and the script, so the script is the artifact worth keeping in
# history and half a megabyte of MP4 per run is not.
/hexhound-demo-*.mp4
/hexhound-demo-*.gif
LANE_*_CALLSITE.md
